[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-246720"] :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=10$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{x}_{i}=-110,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot (-110) \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{x}_{i}^{2}=1\\,350,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot 1350 \\\\  & =135.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =135-{(-11)}^{2} \\\\  & =135-121 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-263257/field-1/fe57a98a9c6478ab0503b1ddf137d76366614cd0146a37e500484adb2ba60e15" :answer/id #uuid "5635cbe5-baa1-52c2-a4cc-627869cb0591" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263257/field-1/8102a39f7519f98a2b41a164242b38d40d9ee8d85b77838c46de229162bb3024" :answer/id #uuid "bdb66389-ff3e-5b1c-a505-e2be3bdfeafc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263257/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d5e2ddd-96c4-5c5d-847f-d583fda88aa3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263257/field-1/fe57a98a9c6478ab0503b1ddf137d76366614cd0146a37e500484adb2ba60e15" :answer-field/choices ["q-263257/field-1/fe57a98a9c6478ab0503b1ddf137d76366614cd0146a37e500484adb2ba60e15" "q-263257/field-1/8102a39f7519f98a2b41a164242b38d40d9ee8d85b77838c46de229162bb3024"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263257" :question/id #uuid "14f344a6-c26a-52b2-b90a-ff911d074c1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-263257" :question/problem "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n9,\\,13,\\,2,\\,14,\\,7\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=5$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (9+13+2+14+7) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 45 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot ({9}^{2}+{13}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{14}^{2}+{7}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (81+169+4+196+49) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 499 \\\\  & =\\frac{499}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{499}{5}-{(9)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{499}{5}-81 \\\\  & =\\frac{499-405}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{94}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-263257/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0040fc1-2134-5eaa-a3e8-6c7a457f75f5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263257"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263302/field-1/ac46d580a95a8fc03d1a7cb07de70e107b73fba6bf1bc1d13103b84eff3df012" :answer/id #uuid "cd412357-91e3-516c-a16f-fb353f7b405e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263302/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "308fa936-a4a4-5d24-add8-67e18ad4d7a0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263302/field-1/ac46d580a95a8fc03d1a7cb07de70e107b73fba6bf1bc1d13103b84eff3df012" :answer-field/choices ["q-263302/field-1/ac46d580a95a8fc03d1a7cb07de70e107b73fba6bf1bc1d13103b84eff3df012"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263302" :question/id #uuid "966ad440-06bf-5d4f-8138-68d430887a3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-263302" :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $7$ data points, where\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}=63,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2}=686.\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}=63,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (63) \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2}=686,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 686 \\\\  & =98.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =98-{(9)}^{2} \\\\  & =98-81 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-263302/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263302"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263417/field-1/13b89fe5f85f54ae9d7156f3d953abbc3e23748858d17af99b46ee1780343e2c" :answer/id #uuid "c15a5082-b60f-54b5-aedd-9c6ef3ede6a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{188}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186112566 :answer-field/choices ["q-263417/field-1/13b89fe5f85f54ae9d7156f3d953abbc3e23748858d17af99b46ee1780343e2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-263417"] :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (3+18+11+8+7+18+12) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 77 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot ({3}^{2}+{18}^{2}+{11}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{18}^{2}+{12}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (9+324+121+64+49+324+144) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 1035 \\\\  & =\\frac{1035}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1035}{7}-{(11)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1035}{7}-121 \\\\  & =\\frac{1035-847}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{188}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-263590/field-1/c2d7619667f0c196612c5df8dd891fd3654b5471493b36842675ea16c436bb2b" :answer/id #uuid "a6f6c451-8690-5f87-849a-14dff4dcf919" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{414}{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263590/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a826ff53-6286-5948-9661-ba07bab6d886" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263590/field-1/c2d7619667f0c196612c5df8dd891fd3654b5471493b36842675ea16c436bb2b" :answer-field/choices ["q-263590/field-1/c2d7619667f0c196612c5df8dd891fd3654b5471493b36842675ea16c436bb2b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263590" :question/id #uuid "5412ac53-9404-5de6-9901-9a9eedb9bc08" :question/math-academy-id "q-263590" :question/problem "Compute the standard deviation $\\sigma $ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n-11,\\,2,\\,1,\\,9,\\,-10,\\,1,\\,-13\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (-11+2+1+9-10+1-13) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (-21) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot [(-11)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{9}^{2}+(-10)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-13)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot [121+4+1+81+100+1+169] \\\\  & =\\frac{477}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{477}{7}-{(-3)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{477}{7}-9 \\\\  & =\\frac{477-63}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{414}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{\\frac{46}{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-263590/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a72dae6-2bbf-5e59-b71d-8ee57f589753"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263590"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
